<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>UniTN Cybersecurity</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/</link><description>Recent content on UniTN Cybersecurity</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 11:18:04 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Sistemi Operativi</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/sistemi-operativi/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/sistemi-operativi/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="abstract"&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Obiettivo dell&amp;rsquo;insegnamento è quello di fornire i concetti fondamentali che sono alla base dei moderni sistemi operativi, con particolare enfasi sulla gestione della concorrenza, della memoria e del file system. Ogni concetto sarà trattato dal punto di vista teorico. Per i concetti più importanti, la trattazione riguarderà anche aspetti più pratici, in modo da familiarizzare con la loro complessità realizzativa.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Network Security</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/network-security/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/network-security/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="abstract"&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The course aims to present and make students understand the technological, infrastructural, and in part, also economic issues related to computer network security. The course covers both the defensive and attacking aspects of network security. The course also covers a practical part, to allow students to immediately apply some of the acquired knowledge. The practical part also covers soft skills as well at the ability to communicate and present technical work to peers.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Ethical Hacking</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/ethical-hacking/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/ethical-hacking/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="abstract"&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The aim of the teaching is for students to experience the most common techniques and strategies used to build computer attacks, detect them, and analyze their behavior with the final goal of learning how to prevent or mitigate such attacks. A further aim of the course is to develop skills in communicating and presenting one&amp;rsquo;s work to colleagues.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>CyberChallenge.IT</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/cyberchallenge/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/cyberchallenge/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="capture-the-flag-activity-at-unitn"&gt;Capture the Flag activity at UniTN&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We participate in the &lt;a href="https://cyberchallenge.it/"&gt;CyberChallenge.IT programme&lt;/a&gt; 2027; registrations open in December. We run a training programme for a selected number of students.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Lectures take place in DISI rooms. Students admitted to the programme receive an email with further details; additional information is available on the &lt;a href="https://cyberchallenge.it/venues/unitn"&gt;UniTN venue page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>eCTF</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/ectf/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/teaching/ectf/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://ectf.mitre.org/"&gt;eCTF&lt;/a&gt; is managed at UniTN by Luigi Dell&amp;rsquo;Eva.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>When POST Becomes GET: Investigating HTTP Method Interchangeability and Its Security Implications</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/when-post-becomes-get-investigating-http-method-interchangeability-and-its-security-implications/</link><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 11:18:04 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/when-post-becomes-get-investigating-http-method-interchangeability-and-its-security-implications/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Web Cache Overflow: Exploiting Imprecise Keys for Cache Degradation and Beyond</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/web-cache-overflow-exploiting-imprecise-keys-for-cache-degradation-and-beyond/</link><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 11:18:04 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/web-cache-overflow-exploiting-imprecise-keys-for-cache-degradation-and-beyond/</guid><description/></item><item><title>PoME: Distributed Execution Proofs for Modern Microservices</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/pome-distributed-execution-proofs-for-modern-microservices/</link><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 11:18:04 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/pome-distributed-execution-proofs-for-modern-microservices/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Mitigating Code Injection Attacks on Modern GPUs</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/gpu-code-injection/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/gpu-code-injection/</guid><description/></item><item><title>N00B: Bounds Checking for the Masses</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/n00b/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/n00b/</guid><description/></item><item><title>TAGShield: Persistent Tagging for Robust Stack Memory Error Protection</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/tagshield/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/tagshield/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Hidden Web Caches Discovery</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/hidden-web-caches-discovery/</link><pubDate>Tue, 23 Jul 2024 11:18:04 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/hidden-web-caches-discovery/</guid><description/></item><item><title>OAuth 2.0 Redirect URI Validation Falls Short Literally</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/oauth-2.0-redirect-uri-validation-falls-short-literally/</link><pubDate>Tue, 19 Sep 2023 10:41:53 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/oauth-2.0-redirect-uri-validation-falls-short-literally/</guid><description/></item><item><title>ESORICS 2023</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/news/esorics-2023/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Sep 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/news/esorics-2023/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We will be at &lt;a href="https://esorics2023.org/"&gt;ESORICS 2023&lt;/a&gt; in The Hague between September 25–29, 2023 to present our latest research.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Nonce-nce of Web Security: An Investigation of CSP Nonces Reuse</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/the-nonce-nce-of-web-security-an-investigation-of-csp-nonces-reuse/</link><pubDate>Thu, 24 Aug 2023 11:58:46 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/the-nonce-nce-of-web-security-an-investigation-of-csp-nonces-reuse/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Mind the CORS</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/mind-the-cors/</link><pubDate>Thu, 24 Aug 2023 11:49:29 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/mind-the-cors/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Paper accepted at WASP 2023</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/news/nonce-nce-wasp-2023/</link><pubDate>Wed, 02 Aug 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/news/nonce-nce-wasp-2023/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Our paper &lt;a href="https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/the-nonce-nce-of-web-security-an-investigation-of-csp-nonces-reuse/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Nonce-nce of Web Security: an Investigation of CSP Nonces Reuse&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was accepted at the &lt;a href="https://wasp-workshop.github.io/"&gt;WASP workshop&lt;/a&gt; at &lt;a href="https://esorics2023.org/"&gt;ESORICS 2023&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Mind the CORS accepted at IEEE TPS 2023</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/news/mind-the-cors-tps-2023/</link><pubDate>Tue, 01 Aug 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/news/mind-the-cors-tps-2023/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Our paper &lt;strong&gt;Mind the CORS&lt;/strong&gt; was accepted at &lt;a href="https://www.sis.pitt.edu/lersais/conference/tps/2023/index.html"&gt;IEEE TPS 2023&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/author/matteo-golinelli/"&gt;Matteo Golinelli&lt;/a&gt; will be at &lt;a href="https://www.sis.pitt.edu/lersais/conference/tps/2023/index.html"&gt;IEEE TPS 2023&lt;/a&gt; in Atlanta between November 1–3, 2023 to present &lt;a href="https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/mind-the-cors/"&gt;Mind the CORS&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Web Cache Deception Escalates!</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/wcde/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 May 2022 17:40:06 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/wcde/</guid><description/></item><item><title>PISTIS: Trusted Computing Architecture for Low-end Embedded Systems</title><link>https://CybersecurityUnitn.github.io/publication/277124/</link><pubDate>Fri